{#- The game's name, lettered on an order ticket (owner 2026-11-24, option B
    of three): the cream slip from the rail, tilted as if just pinned up, its
    number in the corner, the name in Playfair italic and a red rule under it
    like the paper screens'. The bottom edge is torn. Used on the title
    screen (play.njk), the share picture and the launch post, and copied into
    the video's end card (CafeWork video-tools/order-up/overlays.js), so it
    looks the same everywhere. Change it here, and there.

    Sized by the font-size of whatever holds it: 1em is the size of the name.
    Its styles come with it, so it can be dropped into any page once. -#}
<style>
  .ou-logo { display: inline-block; transform: rotate(-2.5deg); filter: drop-shadow(.07em .08em 0 rgba(31, 69, 82, .35)); line-height: 1; text-align: left; }
  .ou-logo-slip {
    display: block; background: #FAF7F2; color: #22323A; padding: .2em .52em .34em; border-radius: .1em .1em 0 0;
    -webkit-mask: linear-gradient(#000 0 0) top / 100% calc(100% - .14em) no-repeat, radial-gradient(circle .14em at .14em 100%, transparent .13em, #000 .14em) bottom / .28em .14em repeat-x;
            mask: linear-gradient(#000 0 0) top / 100% calc(100% - .14em) no-repeat, radial-gradient(circle .14em at .14em 100%, transparent .13em, #000 .14em) bottom / .28em .14em repeat-x;
  }
  .ou-logo-no { display: block; font: 700 .24em/1 Lato, sans-serif; letter-spacing: .24em; text-transform: uppercase; color: #2C5E70; margin-bottom: .3em; }
  .ou-logo-name { display: block; font: italic 700 1em/1.05 "Playfair Display", Georgia, serif; white-space: nowrap; }
  .ou-logo-rule { display: block; height: .075em; background: #C0392F; margin-top: .1em; border-radius: .04em; }
</style>
<span class="ou-logo" role="img" aria-label="Order Up"><span class="ou-logo-slip" aria-hidden="true"><span class="ou-logo-no">#1 · To go</span><span class="ou-logo-name">Order Up</span><span class="ou-logo-rule"></span></span></span>
